{"agent_id":"6Vw9","agent_seq":1126,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T06:01:48.516904205Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3ce0144f-77d7-4257-acd1-281a343f47af","comment_uuid":"8215f679-97ca-4994-955c-13f31cf61000","author":"6Vw9","content":"Preferred design: bind a live RunBudgetAuthority to every ToolRunContext/RunContext. The authority owns one mutex-protected hierarchical ledger, cancellation-aware elapsed deadlines, child scopes, and RAII call reservations; each reservation atomically checks all ancestors before charging turns/provider calls/tool calls/retries/input/output/fixed-point cost and leasing concurrency, then reconciles exact usage or retains the conservative reservation when usage is unknown. Production top-level runs derive limits from typed session config; resumed/frontend/subagent/MCP children share and narrow the same ledger. Provider helpers clamp output before dispatch and retain model/provider/price-manifest provenance; ToolExecutor, hooks, MCP, subprocesses, VDD, and child admission consume the same run handle. Alternative rejected: frontend-local post-response StopConditions counters cannot prevent overshoot or concurrent races and would preserve semantic drift. Exclusions: do not activate the dormant scheduler, redesign process supervision, or absorb S-057/S-066/S-084; wire current production paths without removing intended capabilities.","created_at":"2026-08-23T06:01:48.514333682Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAPRmFrA7PlrHAnNAJb0W23vNxXTY968MF3AeDVsiBVqrFStnAU+MruEjl6tkkNGUraJ4sryaKf7X2kOYdn2iiBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAA